{"id": "EUVD-2026-97495", "enisaUuid": "9c0e262b-f243-3f96-b0b5-18ceb921adc3", "description": "Gumlet php-image-resize before 3.0.1 contains a denial of service vulnerability because the ImageResize constructor in lib/ImageResize.php passes images to GD imagecreatefrom* functions without pixel limits. Remote attackers can upload small, highly compressed images that decode to large bitmaps, exhausting PHP memory and terminating the worker process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T15:16:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:20:30", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gumlet/php-image-resize/security/advisories/GHSA-3g9v-hjrx-mg5h", "https://github.com/gumlet/php-image-resize/commit/10c1f386e672536d82be0f39b236a80d87767a50", "https://github.com/gumlet/php-image-resize/commit/cd01c9e8aa2382211d760c825799c8102987a8c2", "https://github.com/gumlet/php-image-resize/blob/3.0.0/lib/ImageResize.php#L122-L163", "https://github.com/gumlet/php-image-resize/releases/tag/3.0.1", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gumlet-php-image-resize-before-3.0.1-denial-of-service-via-decompression-bombs"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109398", "GHSA-f678-5vxr-2r99"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1738c521-02a5-3a8b-9c19-bd4f99a6740f", "product": {"name": "php-image-resize", "vendor": {"name": "gumlet"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "642c52a4-0f9e-39f2-b854-50045ba2c0bc", "vendor": {"name": "gumlet"}}], "isExploited": false}